# mm.parse

Shared character-level shell scanning: source spans, token kinds, dialect
flags, character-class predicates, and a stateless cursor that advances over
source text and reports token boundaries through a function-pointer Sink.

The embedded dialect (mm.shell level-1) produces WordFragments and treats
\r\n and bare \r as line endings. The full dialect (mm.shell.full level-3)
produces no fragments and treats \r as blank. Both dialects share the
cursor, the predicates, and the dollar/quote skipping.

This module has no use: edge: it needs the standard library and nothing in
the tree.
